        {
          "id": 2346896592,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "For protocols, `enabled_protocols` contains all the disabled by default protocols that are enabled, and `disabled_protocols` contains all the enabled by default protocols that are disabled. For heuristic dissectors, the `heuristic_protocols` file contains all known heuristics and its status.\n\nThe implication is that if the default enabled flag of a protocol changes, that affects everyone, but if the default for an existing heuristic dissector is changed, anyone who had a saved heuristics dissectors preference file doesn't get the new default value (because there was already a saved enabled status value in the file.)\n\nWe could possibly do something to make the heuristic file more like other prefs and not write anything for dissectors with the default status, so that changes to the default would take effect.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
