      "title": "HiPerConTracer: Disable UDP and TCP heurisics by default",
      "message": "HiPerConTracer: Disable UDP and TCP heurisics by default\n\nNow that the HiPerConTracer dissector allows nanosecond timestamps\n(commit 84df2b629ddf2a569f6d046d6e243f6fc279933b), the heuristic\nis very weak. Previously, the 8 bytes that could contain the timestamp\nhad to be plausible as microseconds, specifically being between\n1238799600000000 and 3889637999999999, or 0.01437% of the search space.\nNow that nanoseconds are also allowed, values between 1238799600000000000\nand 3889637999999999000 are allowed, which is 14.37% of the search\nspace.\n\nThat's too many false positives to enable by default on UDP and TCP.\nDisable it until a more discriminating heuristic is available.\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2025-02-12T12:16:15.000-05:00",
